Description: Integrated open data fixtures used by the 'rmorie' package for examples,
    vignettes, and tests. Contains snapshots of publicly available datasets
    from open-data portals built on the Comprehensive Knowledge Archive
    Network ('CKAN', <https://ckan.org/>), 'Socrata'
    (<https://dev.socrata.com/>), and 'Opendatasoft'
    (<https://www.huwise.com/>) (Chicago, New York City, Toronto, Vancouver,
    and others), Statistics Canada Canadian Centre for Justice and Community
    Safety Statistics ('CCJS') tables, a multi-agent-reviewed corpus of
    Ontario Special Investigations Unit ('SIU', <https://www.siu.on.ca/>)
    director's reports, and synthetic fixtures for unit tests. Also ships a
    small set of disclosure-control helpers for aggregate releases:
    differential privacy (an exact discrete Laplace sampler for counts and
    the analytic Gaussian mechanism for means, drawing on the operating
    system's random source, with privacy-budget accounting), k-anonymity and
    l-diversity checks, and cell suppression audited for exact recovery from
    the margins.
